  "question": {
    "text": "A potential difference of <math><mn>220</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math> is applied across a rheostat of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>12000</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Ω</mi></math>. The voltmeter <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math> has a resistance of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6000</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Ω</mi></math> and distance <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>BC</mi></math>&nbsp;is one-fourth of the distance from <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> to <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math> . The error in the reading of voltmeter is approximately -<br />\r<br />\r<img alt=\"\" height=\"142\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/ci/image24-8295bfc6-f2ba-4c7c-848a-78bbcb40ca65.jpg\" style=\"max-width:\"100%\"; object-fit:contain\" width=\"293\" />",
